		+ "ada plans, builder builds, verifier verifies, reviewer reviews, rebaser rebases, bilal"
		+ "reports, mina triages, rulewriter writes rules, explorer explores"
	SPEC "a role file is Markdown: a front matter between two --- lines, one key: value per line,"
		+ "declaring name, slot, reasoning, capabilities comma-separated, budget and returns, then"
		+ "the system prompt body"
	SPEC "a slot resolves in order to a file of $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/roles/, then to the AGENT"
		+ "entity of the configured instructions corpus that the slot table of config.toml binds to"
		+ "it, then to the built-in role; on a machine that configures neither, every slot resolves"
		+ "to its built-in role"
	SPEC "an AGENT entity is read through awawa at each resolution, never cached: WORK, REASONING,"
		+ "CAPABILITY, BUDGET and RETURNS fill the front matter and its awawa context package is"
		+ "the body; an AGENT entity no row of the slot table names takes no slot"
	SPEC "brigade roles list prints the slot, the role, its source and the model the configured"
		+ "client adapter binds, text and --json; brigade roles show <slot> prints the resolved"
		+ "file"
	SPEC "brigade roles lint fails, naming the file and the key, on a role file that names a model,"
		+ "lacks a declared key, carries an unknown one or a value outside its set"
	SPEC "brigade doctor reports the configured instructions corpus as optional, awawa lint"
		+ "--strict clean or not; none configured is a warning with its fallback, built-in roles"
		+ "and no instructions package"
